        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-12">
        
        <!-- Milestone 1 -->
        <article class="p-8 sm:p-10 rounded-3xl bg-[#FAF7F2] border border-[#EFE7DF] transition-all hover:border-[#E5D6C7]">
          <div class="flex items-baseline gap-4 mb-3">
            <span class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-primary">01</span>
            <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-text-primary">
              Analog-First Learning by Default
            </h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-lg text-text-primary font-medium mb-4">
            Physical books and handwriting first. Devices only when a lesson specifically requires digital tools.
          </p>
          <div class="text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed space-y-2 border-t border-[#E5D6C7]/60 pt-4">
            <p>
              Reading physical books and writing by hand significantly increases comprehension, memory retention, and mental focus.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Milestone 2 -->
        <article class="p-8 sm:p-10 rounded-3xl bg-[#FAF7F2] border border-[#EFE7DF] transition-all hover:border-[#E5D6C7]">
          <div class="flex items-baseline gap-4 mb-3">
            <span class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-primary">02</span>
            <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-text-primary">
              Transparent Device Screen Time Tracking
            </h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-lg text-text-primary font-medium mb-4">
            Measure how much time students actually spend on school screens, and share the data with parents.
          </p>
          <div class="text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed border-t border-[#E5D6C7]/60 pt-4">
            <p>
              Modeled after the Los Angeles Unified School District: we currently have no data on total daily device exposure in Hopewell classrooms.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Milestone 3 -->
        <article class="p-8 sm:p-10 rounded-3xl bg-[#FAF7F2] border border-[#EFE7DF] transition-all hover:border-[#E5D6C7]">
          <div class="flex items-baseline gap-4 mb-3">
            <span class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-primary">03</span>
            <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-text-primary">
              Daily Grade-Level Screen Time Limits
            </h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-lg text-text-primary font-medium mb-6">
            Establish healthy, enforceable daily limits across each grade tier:
          </p>
          
          <!-- Open Typographic Tier Matrix -->
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-6 py-4 border-t border-b border-[#E5D6C7]/60 mb-6">
            <div class="text-left sm:text-center">
              <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider font-bold text-text-secondary mb-1">PreK &ndash; 2nd Grade</div>
              <div class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-primary mb-1">0 Minutes</div>
              <div class="text-xs text-text-secondary">Fully screen-free primary learning</div>
            </div>
            <div class="text-left sm:text-center sm:border-l sm:border-r sm:border-[#E5D6C7]/60 sm:px-4">
              <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider font-bold text-text-secondary mb-1">3rd &ndash; 5th Grade</div>
              <div class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-primary mb-1">&le; 30 Min / Day</div>
              <div class="text-xs text-text-secondary">Occasional instructional use only</div>
            </div>
            <div class="text-left sm:text-center">
              <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider font-bold text-text-secondary mb-1">6th &ndash; 12th Grade</div>
              <div class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-primary mb-1">&le; 45 Min / Day*</div>
              <div class="text-xs text-text-secondary">Balanced middle &amp; high school cap</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="text-xs text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
            <strong class="text-primary">* Reasonable exemptions apply:</strong> Courses where technology is the core subject (Computer Science, Robotics, Keyboarding, Digital Art) are exempt. Case-by-case academic exceptions permitted.
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Milestone 4 -->
        <article class="p-8 sm:p-10 rounded-3xl bg-[#FAF7F2] border border-[#EFE7DF] transition-all hover:border-[#E5D6C7]">
          <div class="flex items-baseline gap-4 mb-3">
            <span class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-primary">04</span>
            <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-text-primary">
              End Routine Take-Home Chromebooks
            </h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-lg text-text-primary font-medium mb-4">
            Homework should be analog by default. Devices stay at school unless a family requests otherwise.
          </p>
          <div class="text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed border-t border-[#E5D6C7]/60 pt-4">
            <blockquote class="italic text-text-primary mb-2">
              &ldquo;Mandatory take-home devices can function as an educational Trojan horse, bringing digital distraction into our homes under the mantle of required homework&mdash;undermining bedtime, outdoor play, and family dinners.&rdquo;
            </blockquote>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Milestone 5 -->
        <article class="p-8 sm:p-10 rounded-3xl bg-[#FAF7F2] border border-[#EFE7DF] transition-all hover:border-[#E5D6C7]">
          <div class="flex items-baseline gap-4 mb-3">
